// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | CURRENT_DECISIONS
// task: ADR-057 System Health API + ADR-058 BE Agent Chat Service | date: 2026-04-06

#what_changed
=Backend (Sonnet T01–T13):
  SystemHealthService: aggregates NATS (stream/consumer stats), Redis (ping/memory), BullMQ (queue counts), MongoDB (isMaster + replicaSet), gateway counts per type (5 managers now export getConnectedCount())
  GET /health/system: 200 response with {nats,redis,bullmq,mongodb,gateways,overall,timestamp}; Admin+SuperAdmin RBAC gate
  BeAgentService: OpenAI-compatible adapter (openai npm); configurable endpoint/apiKey/model from AI_CHAT_ENDPOINT env or SystemConfig DB; stub mode when endpoint empty (simulated tokens, no crash)
  POST /be-agent/chat: 202 fire-and-forget; Socket.io room subscribe/unsubscribe for requestId; be_agent module gate via requireModule() middleware
  WebSocket: added subscribe:be-agent / unsubscribe:be-agent handlers; broadcast be-agent:token with {requestId,token,done,error?}
  config.ts: new ai block (endpoint, apiKey, model) exported in destructure
  .env.example: added AI_CHAT_* stubs with endpoint/key/model descriptions + Ollama/vLLM/Azure examples

=Frontend (Haiku T14–T15):
  useSystemHealth hook: 30s refetch, 5s staleTime; queryKey factory; error-safe
  /system-health page: 5 status cards (NATS/Redis/BullMQ/MongoDB/Gateways); green/amber/red badge per subsystem; overall status banner; Admin+ gate (redirects non-Admin to /dashboard)
  Sidebar: new "System Health" nav link (SuperAdmin only)
  useBeAgentChat hook: generateRequestId, sendMessage(message, deviceId?), streaming token listener, clearChat cleanup; non-blocking Socket.io room joins
  /admin-management: new "BE Agent AI Configuration" section (endpoint/apiKey/model inputs, current config display, Save + loading state, success toast); useBeAgentConfig() + useUpdateBeAgentConfig() mutations

#tech_implications
~SystemHealthService is read-only aggregation: no DB writes, no side effects; each check isolated (failure in one doesn't crash others)
~openai npm supports all OpenAI-compatible endpoints (Ollama, vLLM, Azure, Groq, OpenRouter, etc.) via baseURL override — no vendor lock-in
~Stub mode: AI_CHAT_ENDPOINT="" → simulated streaming (no external calls, testing-friendly); graceful fallback when endpoint unset
~Socket.io be-agent:token events: requestId-based room isolation (multiple concurrent chats); fire-and-forget POST contract (202) eliminates blocking; frontend manages stream collection lifecycle
~requireModule('be_agent') checks ModuleConfig singleton at route gate; dev override (NODE_ENV=development) → all modules enabled (mirrors ADR-051 frontend behaviour)
~optionalDependencies: node-bacnet/node-ethernet-ip moved (dynamic import pattern — server boots even if packages not installed); reduces node_modules bloat
~Both gateways (BACnet, EtherNet/IP) now expose getConnectedCount() for system-health aggregation (parity with Modbus/OPC-UA/MQTT)

#constraints
~System health endpoint 30s poll interval — choose 30s as balance (not too frequent to stress infra, not too stale for ops visibility); can be tuned via useSystemHealth(pollInterval) param
~BE Agent config stored in SystemConfig (MongoDB) — runtime-mutable (no Docker rebuild); but no versioning/audit of config changes (acceptable for Phase 1; Phase 2 can add ConfigHistory)
~Streaming via Socket.io be-agent:token — requires Socket.io connection; fallback: HTTP long-poll if needed (future enhancement)
~be_agent module gate: platform-level, not per-user; all licensed users get same module set (multi-tenant model deferred)
~Stub mode replies are fixed English text; Phase 2 can add locale/i18n if needed
~System health cards show latest snapshot only (no historical trends); metrics stored in Redis (short TTL) — no time-series history of health status
~Gateway getConnectedCount() returns instantaneous count; gateways can flap online/offline rapidly — count is point-in-time (smooth animations on frontend suggested)

#scope
~arch_summary_update: already done (ADR-057/058 entries added in earlier edit)
